{"id":"s2","level":5,"levelName":"Structure and style","n":2,"of":6,"title":"If","titleHe":"תְּנַאי","goal":"Tell a real condition from an impossible one.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"אִם is for things that might happen, and takes the future. לוּ and אִילוּ are for things that didn't, and take the past — with הָיָה carrying the counterfactual."},{"type":"examples","items":[{"he":"אִם יִהְיֶה זְמַן, נֵלֵךְ.","en":"If there's time, we'll go."},{"he":"אִילוּ יָדַעְתִּי, הָיִיתִי בָּא.","en":"Had I known, I would have come."},{"he":"לוּ הָיָה לִי כֶּסֶף…","en":"If only I had money…"}]},{"type":"tip","body":"The counterfactual is built with הָיָה plus the present participle: הָיִיתִי בָּא, I would have come. It's the one place the present tense is used to talk about the past."}],"vocab":[{"he":"אִם","en":"if","translit":"im"},{"he":"אִילוּ","en":"if (contrary to fact)","translit":"ilu"},{"he":"אוּלַי","en":"maybe","translit":"ulai"},{"he":"בְּלִי","en":"without","translit":"bli"},{"he":"אַף עַל פִּי כֵן","en":"nevertheless","translit":"af al pi chen"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["if","mouth","maybe","her"],"correct":0,"prompt":"אִם","translit":"im"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["explained","if (contrary to fact)","where","old (of things)"],"correct":1,"prompt":"אִילוּ","translit":"ilu"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["maybe","very","sea","certainly"],"correct":0,"prompt":"אוּלַי","translit":"ulai"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["our","never","uncle","without"],"correct":3,"prompt":"בְּלִי","translit":"bli"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["nevertheless","to come","and he said","is finished"],"correct":0,"prompt":"אַף עַל פִּי כֵן","translit":"af al pi chen"},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “if (contrary to fact)”?","options":["טוֹב","אִילוּ","עוֹשֶׂה","הַתְחָלָה"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"“Had I known, I would have come.”","options":["אִילוּ יָדַעְתִּי, הָיִיתִי בָּא","אִם יָדַעְתִּי, אָבוֹא","אִם אֵדַע, בָּאתִי","אִילוּ אֵדַע, אֲנִי בָּא"],"correct":0,"why":"A condition that didn't happen takes אִילוּ with the past, and הָיָה plus the participle in the result."},{"type":"match","pairs":[["בְּלִי","without"],["אִם","if"],["אִילוּ","if (contrary to fact)"],["אוּלַי","maybe"],["אַף עַל פִּי כֵן","nevertheless"]]},{"type":"read","he":"בְּלִי","translit":"bli","en":"without"},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["אִילוּ","אוּלַי","אַף עַל פִּי כֵן","אִם"],"correct":1,"say":"אוּלַי","he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “nevertheless”?","options":["אַף עַל פִּי כֵן","בֵּין","נִכְנָס","שֶׁל"],"correct":0,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “without”?","options":["אַל","בְּלִי","הַיּוֹם","לָהּ"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “if”?","options":["מֶלֶךְ","אִם","לָמָּה","מְקַבֵּל"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"type","q":"Write “if” in Hebrew","answer":"אִם","hint":"im"}]}